  "note": [
    "The Reactor Access Stairs's fabric (DR-106, the mech wing), cut from the one Kalamontee layout in scripts/fabric-kalamontee.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. A spiral stair in a 3.6 m square concrete shaft north of Reactor Control, built from parts ('open'): five turns of 16 treads round a steel post, the top tread level with Reactor Control's floor inside the doorway. The eye stands on the tread at bearing 312.5 from the axis, 2.2 m under Reactor Control's floor, 1 m out from the post (the metadata's eye: [-0.737, 1.6, -0.676] in this frame, whose origin is the axis at that tread's level).",
    "Dark (no ONBIT, compone.zil 1477; its LDESC is \"You have just located a serious bug\"): its paintings show it lit by the lamp the player carries, as the Transportation Supply's do, so this scene takes a warm light at the eye with no housing. UP, the stair climbs round to the 1.4 x 2.3 doorway, Reactor Control's lit ceiling and south wall beyond it; DOWN, the stair winds on into the dark -- DOWN leads back to this same room (1475)."
